## Fixes 1 + 2 (import), by task agent ImportSemantics
RED: `cargo test -p aperture-import --no-fail-fast`
  -> normal_cards 0 passed/6 failed; normalize_real 1 failed; plan 5 passed/1 failed; url_guard 4/1
GREEN: `cargo test -p aperture-import --no-fail-fast`
  -> normal_cards 6 passed; normalize_real 2; plan 6; text_import 4; url_guard 5; 0 failed (23 passed)
  `cargo fmt -p aperture-import` (exit 0), re-ran: all pass.
Root causes fixed: (a) `classify` rejected every entry with `faces == []` as "no card data" even
for layout "normal" cards whose metadata is on oracleCard; now only a genuinely empty name is
"no provider data", and multi-face/meld layouts still refuse. (b) `normalize` clamped quantity to
u8 and silently skipped 0; now a missing/non-integer/0/>255 quantity is an ImportError::Parse with
the value, and exact values are retained. (c) `parse_deck_url` refused the canonical
/decks/<id>/<human_slug> link form; now one optional non-authoritative slug segment is accepted,
still built into the API URL from the numeric id only.
Note: two pre-existing assertions were provably invalid and were updated with comments saying why
(url_guard's '/decks/26206384/extra' rejection; normalize_real's "no card data" reason) —
the real cached deck's faceless entries are 13 normal-layout cards (pool reason) + 2 meld-layout
cards (multi-face reason).

## Fixes 5 + 6 (ai/decider), by task agent AiDecider
RED: `cargo test -p aperture-ai --test decider_usage`
  -> after adding only the new error variant: 3 failed / 1 passed
     * P1 viewer saw life P1 == 3 (should be 17)
     * choose() returned a ChoiceAnswer for a response with usage.truncated == true
     * DeciderPolicy returned DecisionSource::Decider for the truncated response
GREEN: `cargo test -p aperture-ai`
  -> decider 4, decider_redirect 1, decider_usage 4, heuristic 11, selfplay 3; 23 passed; 0 failed
Root causes fixed: (a) `decision_request` keyed `life` with a P0/P1 literal that is only correct for
a P0 viewer; now keyed by the real absolute seats. (b) `choose` ignored usage.truncated /
state_tokens_dropped / truncated_questions; now any of them yields DeciderError::Truncated and the
policy falls back to the visible heuristic instead of using a choice the model made without seeing
the whole projection.

## Fixes 3 + 4 (UI vertical path + async), integration owner
RED: `git stash push -- crates/ui/src/{session,app,main}.rs && cargo test -p aperture-ui --test import_and_async`
  -> does not compile against the pre-fix API (no `seat_import`, `start_imported_match`,
     `can_start_imported`, `request_import`, `poll_workers`, `import_seat_text`, `load_explicit_deck`):
     a missing-capability RED, recorded here rather than papered over.
GREEN: `cargo test -p aperture-ui`
  -> import_and_async 9 passed; session 7 passed; 0 failed
What the new tests prove:
  * two DISTINCT imported lists (Temur Beats for P0, Izzet Control for P1) actually enter the game
    and the replay snapshots, 7-card hands dealt, revision 0 ("no substitutions").
  * an out-of-pool list for one seat is REFUSED; `can_start_imported()` is false and
    `start_imported_match` is an error that leaves the digest unchanged.
  * the text fallback certifies both seats, and malformed text is refused with a real reason.
  * a missing/invalid explicitly requested deck file yields an empty list plus
    "Refusing to substitute the bundled practice deck" (never the bundled list).
  * an import worker result is applied through `poll_workers`; a missing file path is reported.
  * `poll_workers` returns promptly while a worker is blocked; after the game is replaced with the
    SAME seed the released stale completion is discarded ("stale"), digest/revision/pending/replay
    are all unchanged; a fresh completion is applied (revision advances).
  * `submit_human` refuses to act for the AI seat and says "not your seat".

